  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government continues to implement various measures to strengthen national food security, ranging from regional market initiatives to infrastructure development. Recently, the Jakarta Timur police department facilitated a affordable food market providing two tons of rice at subsidized prices to support local community needs. In connection with these efforts, Perum Bulog President Director Ahmad Rizal Ramdhani explicitly prohibited the trading of government food aid by beneficiaries, emphasizing that these resources are intended for personal consumption. Meanwhile, broader national initiatives include the development of the Rukoh dam by Waskita Karya and efforts by the Ministry of Marine Affairs and Fisheries to promote fish consumption. These interventions occur alongside tracking of commodity price fluctuations, such as the reported increase in red chili prices, as authorities aim to balance supply chain stability and public access to basic staples.",
